CHARACTERIZATION

  Aliases
  - CLI bare view aliases: `topics`, `hubs`, `paths` normalized by
    `tam_addr_cli_alias` in `src/tam.c` (W84). `-` is stdin.
  - `page:` is an explicit guide scheme; stripped by
    `tam_addr_strip_page_prefix` (W85, W87, W89) and accepted by
    `tam_addr_kind` as GUIDE.
  - Action aliases are not parsed as aliases: `tam:help` dispatches to
    `help/index.html`, `tam:start` runs tam-start; both are route-table
    ACTION entries with NULL loader and custom follow() behavior.

  Fold/path params
  - Fold open state is split by `tam_fold_split_href` before corpus page
    load; fold ids are parsed by `tam_addr_fold_id` (W83).
  - Level is split by `tam_depth_split_href` (`?level=`), which also
    tolerates `?path=` but does not return it.
  - Path selection is read separately by `tam_addr_param(href, "path", ...)`
    in `read_corpus_page` (`src/corpus.c`), then used for path navigation
    metadata/body links. Same href may be scanned/split multiple times
    (fold, depth, path param) - duplication remains, but behavior is
    coupled to fold/depth/corpus rendering.

  Relative Guide links
  - Pager follow() handles `#fragment`, tam: actions, and external links;
    other hrefs go through `load_at_lens` -> `tam_address_load` ->
    `tam_corpus_page_document`. Relative guide paths are not resolved in
    pager_nav; they are treated as corpus/page hrefs by the loader/corpus
    path join (`corpus_join` uses `tam_path_join_under` and rejects URL
    schemes). This keeps relative resolution out of pager dispatch.

  External opener confirmation
  - `follow_external` (`src/pager_nav.c`) rejects URLs failing
    `tam_external_url_ok` with malformed/scheme-specific messages.
  - First press on an unopened external href arms `pending_external` and
    reports opener name (`tam_external_opener`); second press on same
    href opens detached (graphical) or foreground (text browser) via
    external.c helpers. Different href re-arms. This is confirmation
    behavior, not address parsing shape.

